  "articleBody": "Knowing when to bring in a professional for your accessible bathroom renovation can save you a lot of headaches and ensure a safe, functional space. Here are some key indicators that it's time to call in the experts:\n\n*   **When structural changes are involved:** If your renovation means moving walls or adding new doorways, you absolutely need a pro to handle the structural integrity.\n*   **If you're dealing with plumbing or waterproofing:** These aren't DIY-friendly jobs. Improper plumbing can lead to leaks, and bad waterproofing can cause serious damage.\n*   **For structural blocking for grab bars:** This is so important for safety! Grab bars need solid support, not just drywall anchors. A professional knows how to properly reinforce walls.\n*   **When code-compliant layout changes are needed:** Accessible design has specific clearance requirements. An experienced remodeler understands ADA-style guidance and local building codes to ensure everything is compliant.\n*   **To avoid unsafe or nonfunctional results:** Ultimately, if you want peace of mind that your accessible bathroom will be safe, functional, and durable, a professional like HH Remodeling LLC, serving the greater Denver area, is your best bet. We make sure it's done right the first time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
